course: dictionary
lesson: 5756
title: Loyalty
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Loyalty means being faithful and supportive to a person, group, team or country, and sticking with them. «Loyalty means being kind to a friend, not covering up harm they did.» A loyal friend stands by you, keeps promises and helps you when things are hard.
explain: Loyalty is a feeling you can have for many things, such as «a sense of loyalty» to your family, your team or your school. The word loyalties (with an s) means the people or things you feel loyal to. A hero in a story might have «divided loyalties» when two people they care about need different things.
explain: Loyalty is good, but not loyalty to wrongdoing. «If you see a friend cheat, loyalty and fairness clash; a good first step is often to talk to your friend.» The clues tell you that loyalty can pull against fairness, so you have to think about what is right.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Shops have «loyalty cards» that give points to customers who come back, so loyalty there is about coming back again and again. Dogs are famous for loyalty because they stay close to their owners. When you meet loyalty, ask: is someone sticking with a person or thing they care about?
fact: Loyalty means being faithful and supportive, and sticking with a person, group, team or country.
fact: Loyalties means the people or things you feel loyal to.
fact: «Loyalty cards» give points to customers who come back to a shop.
fact: «Divided loyalties» means feeling pulled towards two different people or things at the same time.
fact: Being loyal to a friend does not mean covering up harm they did.
exercise: What does loyalty mean? | *Being faithful and supportive, and sticking with someone | Winning every game you play | Telling everyone a secret | Being the fastest runner in the class
exercise: A shop's «loyalty cards» give points to customers. Why are they called loyalty cards? | They are sold for a lot of money | They show the shop's address | They are only for children | *They reward customers who keep coming back
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the people or things you feel loyal to. | victim | *loyalties | fairness | loyalty
test: If you see a friend cheat, what is often a good first step, according to the text? | Ignore it forever | Tell everyone in the class | *Talk to your friend | Keep the secret so you stay loyal
test: A hero has «divided loyalties». What does this mean? | Being loyal to nobody at all | Having two pet dogs | *Feeling pulled towards two people or things at once | Being very good at dividing sweets
exam: What must you do with a secret that puts someone in danger? | Keep it, because loyalty always comes first | Forget it straight away | *Tell a trusted adult | Share it with the whole class
